From 82d8ac0d85a14240a5e290e408cfb19f53712a3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Kenney <dylan@dkenney.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:08:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] service/notifications: send an activation token with
 invoked actions

Request a token with the shared activation helper and send it with the
ActivationToken signal before ActionInvoked, so the sender can raise
its window when it handles the action.

The token arrives asynchronously, and callers often dismiss the
notification right after invoking an action. Closes requested while an
invocation waits for its token are held until ActionInvoked has gone
out, so the client still sees ActionInvoked before NotificationClosed.
